cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CrashDefNet, please cite it as below."
title: "CrashDefNet: Learned Deformation Prediction on Simulation Meshes"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Stocker
    given-names: Felix
    email: felix.stocker@sto-eng.de
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
license: Apache-2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23575635
repository-code: "https://github.com/stofe94/crash-def-net"
abstract: >-
  CrashDefNet is a deep-learning research tool for predicting structural
  deformation from finite element simulations, designed for scientific purposes.
  It covers the chain from raw simulation data to the predicted deformation and
  implements MeshGraphNets and the MeshGraphNet-Transformer (MGN-T) in one
  pipeline, evaluated with the metrics of the MGN-T paper on DeepMind's
  deforming_plate benchmark.
keywords:
  - graph neural networks
  - MeshGraphNets
  - MeshGraphNet-Transformer
  - crash simulation
  - CAE
  - finite element method
  - surrogate model
